# Carnot's theorem (perpendicularity form) — the feet of the perpendiculars from any point to the sides satisfy BFa² + CFb² + AFc² = FaC² + FbA² + FcB² (source: Carnot)
A B C = triangle
P = free
Fa = foot(P, line(B, C))
Fb = foot(P, line(C, A))
Fc = foot(P, line(A, B))
prove dist(B, Fa) ^ 2 + dist(C, Fb) ^ 2 + dist(A, Fc) ^ 2 = dist(Fa, C) ^ 2 + dist(Fb, A) ^ 2 + dist(Fc, B) ^ 2
